bit-loss lemma -- does any mod-2^K class survive one step intact?
     K  odd classes    classes whose images differ mod 2^K
     6           32                                     32
     8          128                                    128
    10          512                                    512
    12         2048                                   2048
    14         8192                                   8192
  every class splits: no finite 2-adic membership is inheritance-stable.

precision budget -- the first L valuations are fixed by m mod 2^{S_L+1}
  70000 (m,L) pairs: 0 failures of sufficiency at modulus 2^(S_L+1)

minimal automaton -- odd residues mod 2^N quotiented by L-step futures
    N   2^(N-1) L=1      L=2      L=4      L=6      L=8      L=10     L=12    
   10       512 10      46      256     466     511     512     512    
   12      2048 12      67      562     1486    1981    2047    2048   
   14      8192 14      92      1093    4096    7099    8100    8191   
   16     32768 16      121     1941    9949    22819   30827   32647  
  saturation at the full 2^(N-1) states: no merging survives.

pinning lemma -- r(w_N(m)) = m for all N >= bitlength(m)
  odd m in [3,4000]: 0 violations; max first-pin step 10 (always <= bitlength(m))
